# Where your Gear 360 may be found: one address per line, tried in this order.
#
# Copy this file to `camera-hosts` (same folder, without ".example") and edit it.
# `camera-hosts` is ignored by git, so your own network stays out of the
# repository. Tools such as tools/observe/camsh.py read it.
#
# 192.168.43.1 is the camera's own Wi-Fi access point; it is fixed by the
# firmware and is always tried last, so you do not need to list it. Add the
# address your router gives the camera once it has joined your network (the
# app's WIFI setting): look in the router's list of clients, or run `arp -a`.
# That address can change; update the file when it does.
#
# 192.168.1.50      # example: the camera on your home network
# 172.20.10.4       # example: the camera on a phone hotspot
